In article <10321@aggie.ucdavis.edu> e5w127@judy.ucdavis.edu () writes:
>1. Why won't my stupid cat follow me downstairs? Was it something I said?
>  It is proving to be most frustrating...

Pets will accompany you down stairways only if they are on a space directly
adjacent to the stairway when you go down it.

>3. How exactly does one set some of the game options, such as naming the 
>  character, and the numberpad option? Is it something I'd type from a
>  UNIX prompt, before starting the game, of would it be a bunch of flags
>  I'd add to the end of the start command, ie
>           prompt---> %nethack -option1 -option2 -option3
>  I have no clue, and I'm sick of being named e5w127. :)

Some options can be set from within the game by using the "O" command and
then typing the option.  Other options have to be set by either using a
setenv NETHACKOPTIONS=options or by using flags to the program.  Consult the
nethack internal documentation (hit "?" from within the game) for more
information.

Oh, and a quickie - to use a different name, type "nethack -uNewname" when
you want to play.  Oh, and one more thing - a lot of systems will let you
type 'man nethack' from your regular shell prompt to get more information
about nethack and the various options for it.

> 4. Finally, where could I find some general instructions (besides the 
>   recently posted spoiler list), so I could answer some of these
>   inane questions myself.

See above.  Either from within the game or by using the man command.

